  "draw": "census: all 95 witnesses of census.json, in order",
  "transcript": "The proposal artifact is canonically serialised as JSON with recursively sorted keys and no whitespace, and those exact bytes are persisted as proposal_canon.json in the run's scratch dir; a third party re-derives hProposal by running sha256sum proposal_canon.json, then re-derives the seed by computing SHA-256 over the concatenation of hProposal and the salt (hProposal + salt), yielding seedHex verbatim as given by the engine; since this is a census draw, no selection or replacement logic applies beyond taking the full, ordered witness bank from census.json — all 95 entries in the order they appear — so the draw itself needs no further randomness once the seed is fixed, and the seed's sole role here is to bind this proposal instance to this witness set for audit purposes."
